# The touchpad on PlayStation 4 and 5 controllers (DualShock 4, DualSense, DualSense Edge) doesn't
# move the desktop's pointer, so resting a thumb on it during a game does nothing outside the game.
# Games still read it: Steam Input and SDL use the controller's raw HID device, not this input
# device, and Steam can map the touchpad to the mouse itself. Matches the touchpad input device
# hid-playstation creates, over a cable ("Sony Interactive Entertainment ... Touchpad") and over
# Bluetooth ("... Wireless Controller Touchpad").
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{id/vendor}=="054c", \
    ATTRS{name}=="*Wireless Controller Touchpad", ENV{LIBINPUT_IGNORE_DEVICE}="1"
